Description: breeze: Declare the depths its shadows do not say
 .
 Breeze's buttons, combo boxes and cards are raised by their own shadows,
 and a pressed, flat or disabled button has none, so it lies flat. A new
 depth.css, imported last, declares the rest of Daniel's rules: what is
 toggled or selected is sunk (checked buttons, the current tab, selected
 rows, but not the current item of a menu or a list), disabled controls
 lie at the screen, a tool button that is not flat is raised as Qt raises
 it, a flat one rises only under the pointer, as Qt's own model does, and
 menus, popups, tooltips and dialogs drawn inside a window are popped, as
 Stereo KWin places those that are surfaces of their own. Breeze's 2D
 look is unchanged.
